<Layout
  title="Tuzdy Currlin, MD"
  description="Tuzdy Currlin, MD — Pediatrician, co-founder of Blessed Are They."
  active="about"
>
  <FounderProfile
    name="Tuzdy Currlin, MD"
    role="Pediatrician · Co-founder"
    photo="/uploads/Tuzdy Currlin, MD.JPG"
    objectPosition="47% 22%"
    bioHtml={[
      'A pediatrician with 10 years of clinical experience, wife, and mother of four. Dr. Tuzdy Currlin brings a deep respect for children, families, and the extraordinary work of growing up.',
      'Across clinical practice, parish ministry, and family life, she has seen that children need clear, trustworthy guidance as they begin to make sense of their bodies, relationships, emotions, and place in the world. Parents need it too: not one more vague message or cultural talking point, but practical formation they can trust and use at home.',
      "Dr. Currlin came to the Catholic faith after years of trying to build a life around the culture's measures of success. In discovering the Church's vision of the human person, she found a more complete answer: each person is created by God, known and loved from the beginning, and made for a purpose no achievement can supply.",
      "That conviction shapes her work with Blessed Are They. She is committed to helping families receive education that is medically responsible, developmentally wise, and grounded in the Catholic understanding of the person — body and soul, created with dignity and called to flourish.",
    ]}
    focusHtml="<b><i>Her focus in Program Development:</i></b><br />Content creation and medical-science oversight — ensuring every lesson is clinically accurate, age-appropriate, clearly communicated, and faithful to the Church's vision of the human person."
  />
</Layout>
